id: eyepatch
name: Eyepatch
kind: gear
itemType: accessory
craftDC: Apprentice
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Perception's Natural Result 1 lower relying on sight; Intimidation's 1 higher.
text: >
  Eyepatch: Created with the intention of hiding a damaged eye, these are often worn by
  fierce warriors or cutthroats; either way, they indicate that the wearer is quite
  dangerous.
  –Craft DC: Apprentice
  –Effects: Decrease the Natural Result of any Perception checks made that rely on sight by
  1, but in return increase the Natural Result of any Intimidation checks by 1.

---

# The Natural Result, not the total: it moves the die a Critical and a Botch are read off.
# Whether a Perception Check relies on sight is the player's to say: the roll asks, while
# this is worn.
[passive]
skill.perception.natural.sight -= 1;
skill.intimidation.natural += 1;
